<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of La Arada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1851</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of La Arada was fought on 2 February 1851 near Chiquimula in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>. Guatemalan forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-carrera">Rafael Carrera</a> routed a larger allied army from El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> and Honduras that had invaded to overthrow him and restore the Central American federation. The victory secured Carrera's conservative regime and Guatemala's independence as a separate republic.</p></div>
